lse}, {"t_ms": 454051, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EV78H9KNLiT5FN5u9SbYVV", "tool": "merge_pr", "args": {"number": 101}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 455251, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EV78H9KNLiT5FN5u9SbYVV", "tool": "merge_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 455251, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EV78H9KNLiT5FN5u9SbYVV", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 459552, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The fix is merged into main and will ship in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/round-half-even-fin-212`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR #101:** The request to open it timed out, but I checked and it had been created, so I didn't open a second one. It was missing a reviewer, so I added `code-owner`.\n- **Merge:** Policy requires a code owner to approve merges into main. You approved, and I merged PR #101.\n\nThis changes how exact half-cent amounts round: 2.665 now becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67. Anything downstream that relied on the old rounding will see different results.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files and the advisory.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UUUog6aG4nBYzis6sNhYB2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}