-212", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` (despite its docstring saying half-even).\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: this changes rounding behavior for exact half-cent amounts (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66 instead of 2.67).", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-round-half-even-fin-212"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I'll check whether the PR got created before trying again.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017gCbKvJv3WHMhdop3sCFFK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "PR #101 was created despite the timeout, but no reviewers were attached. I'll add the reviewer.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YX5A4iWxpg5eJ4EG37jHgm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["code-owner"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Policy says merging into main needs a code owner's approval, and the PR doesn't have one yet. I'll ask for it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01P9UoQ7SPtwBzqN2udAh5H9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"question": "PR #101 (fix/round-half-even-fin-212 -> main) switches round_money from ROUND_HALF_UP to ROUND_HALF_EVEN per FIN-212. That fixes the failing nightly test, and CI run ci-0001 passed on head 08d3cd5986. This changes how exact half-cent amounts round (e.g. 2.665 now gives 2.66, not 2.67). Merging into main needs code-owner approval. Can a code owner approve this merge so it ships in today's release?", "action_tool": "merge_pr", "action_args": {"number": 101}}, "name": "ask_human", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EV78H9KNLiT5FN5u9SbYVV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is merged into main and will ship in today's release.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/round-half-even-fin-212`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR #101:** The request to open it timed out, but I checked and it had been created, so I didn't open a second one. It was missing a reviewer, so I added `code-owner`.\n- **Merge:** Policy requires a code owner to approve merges into main. You approved, and I merged PR #101.\n\nThis changes how exact half-cent amounts round: 2.665 now becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67. Anything downstream that relied on the old rounding will see different results.", "type": "text"}]}]}